WEBVTT

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.990
Special: Merry Christmas!
Christmas is a decisive battle for couples

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.300
"Christmas is a decisive battle for couples."

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.900
Ageha, let us celebrate 
this holy night together.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.170
Rinne, I have a present for you.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.630
That present is

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.620
me!

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.190
I'll get you this eve!

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.360
Prepare yourself, Rinne!

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:22.030
Merry Christmas in the Derelict

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.410
That one.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.790
Give me that one.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.040
This.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.660
I'll have this.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.920
This to this.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.420
All of it.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:33.420
This one.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.630
And that one.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.130
Year-end Sale!

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.390
I'm pretty sure that's everything I need.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.210
Miss, Miss!

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.950
Preparing for Christmas?

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.060
How about this, then?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.310
A Friendly Square.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.810
Friendly Square?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.800
Yes, an intimate quadrangle.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:02.200
It's a deployable Intimacy Field Generator.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.530
Intimacy Field Generator?

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.920
So it lets you make friends with spirits?

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.910
Not just spirits.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.500
Humans and Shinigamis, too.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.120
Bring them into the space 
and it's happy times!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.300
Can Shinigamis get closer to each other, too?

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.820
Especially a man and a woman.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.060
<i>With the new year around the corner, the 
afterlife shops throwing year-end promotions.</i>

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.250
<i>Though the products at these 
shops are generally good,</i>

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.890
<i>a lot of scams show up 
at this time of the year.</i>

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.690
<i>Hardly any Shinigamis ever 
fall for them, however.</i>

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.500
Buy now, and I'll throw in a Quadrangle Pad,

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:45.310
a Field Cage and a Field Plane 
for just one hundred thousand yen.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:46.580
Nice! Sold!

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.450
<i>But once in a while, there's a 
Shinigami that falls for them.</i>

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.830
I'm all set now.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.930
Rinne might be surprised.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.100
This aura...

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.840
Santa-san!

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.600
Over here!

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.610
Convenience Store

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.360
Christmas

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.770
Thank you, come again!

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.560
So you finally bought it, Rinne-sama.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.130
Keep it together, Rokumon.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.970
Are you sure we won't be 
punished for spending so much?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.010
No way.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.010
Christmas Eve comes only once a year.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:55.430
Let's light candles and 
share this cake in style!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.350
Then again, we live in 
candlelight every night.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.160
A letter?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.660
Help me

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.890
A derelict.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.420
Rinne! Yay!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.130
You're here to save me!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.620
Ageha.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.930
Hey! Who told you to leave?

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.490
What's the idea, dressing up so jolly?

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.280
You should go home, too.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.730
What the...

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.020
Do you get it now?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.290
It looks like there's a powerful barrier.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:46.030
We can't get out.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.660
<i>This is an opportunity, though.</i>

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:55.290
Hey, have you heard?

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.320
You know how there's a derelict around here?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.040
Supposedly, back when 
people used to live there,

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:07.050
they set up some spectacular 
Christmas lights every year.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.130
But the whole family moved out one year.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:14.770
Yeah, yeah. Apparently they had to 
sell the house because of the economy.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.810
That must have been disappointing.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.310
Yeah, and maybe it's because 
of the family's regrets;

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.810
the lights come on when there 
isn't supposed to be anyone home.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:37.300
You're right. This used to be a derelict 
when we passed by during the day.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.480
No one lives here, right?

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.930
I'm scared!

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:51.800
<i>Someone's inside?</i>

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.100
Why do you keep running?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.650
Why do you chase me?

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.230
We can't get out anymore.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:06.210
The two of us have to live 
out our days together here.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.890
I'm here too.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.380
What're you doing?

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.570
Mamiya Sakura.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.780
Jeez! Don't come in!

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:17.490
Huh, I'm, like, stuck inside.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.750
So that's how I got lured in.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:26.780
I came in thinking I'd purify them if 
they were having trouble passing on.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.510
But there was no spirit, 
and you couldn't get out.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.510
There's rumors that it's 
because of the regrets of the

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.360
Christmas-loving family 
that used to live here.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.160
That a living spirit did this?

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.350
Nope.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.140
That family moved elsewhere for work,

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.020
and they're having another 
happy Christmas this year.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.230
Tsubasa-kun.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.730
Actually, I came here by 
that family's request.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:54.010
Apparently, they caught wind that this 
house is celebrating Christmas by itself.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:56.830
They wanted me to offer the 
house chicken or something.

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.290
The house?

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.440
So it's a poltergeist caused by the 
house's fond memories of Christmas,

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.080
since it's been left behind.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.380
That settles it, then.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.170
Let's leave some chicken 
and get out of here.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.600
You're a life saver, Tsubasa-kun.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:14.710
Mamiya-san, since we're here, how about 
tonight we go check out the city lights?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.400
Bonked.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.270
Why did you leave it 
outside when you came in?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.480
We can't even open a Reidou from inside.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:29.860
Maybe all the house wants is 
to enjoy a festive Christmas.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.240
I have something perfect for that.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.570
<i>Like what?</i>

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.240
<i>Chicken? Cake?!</i>

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:39.130
Let's see, where did I put it?

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.240
Huh?

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.000
<i>It's a scarf!</i>

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.250
<i>And it looks hand-knit!</i>

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.210
Party goods!

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
What are you freaking out about?

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.630
I'm not freaking out.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:57.060
F-Forget that. Mine's even better.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.140
Behold! The extravagance will blind you.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.730
A turkey? A high-quality whole cake?!

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:10.050
I wanted to spend a 
romantic night with Rinne.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.620
Nothing but candles.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:14.110
It's just like the Hyakumonogatari horror stories.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:18.280
<i>Of all the things that 
you could have brought!</i>

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.080
I'm tired of seeing candles every night.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.960
It's a lot brighter now, though.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.040
Now if only we had a cake or two.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.710
Yeah, cake is a must on Christmas.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.340
<i>Irk!</i>

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.340
Cake!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.930
<i>Wh-What do I do?</i>

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.080
<i>Do I offer it?</i>

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>The five of us are going to share this cake?</i>

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.210
<i>This tiny cake?</i>

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.290
<i>Should I hide it?</i>

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:54.230
<i>But wait, if... If they found out...</i>

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.640
You bastard, you were going 
to keep the cake to yourself?!

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.950
We could have gotten out 
of this house with that!

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:03.850
Rokudou-kun, you're the worst.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.660
The worst.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:07.880
The worst.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.780
The worst.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.460
<i>Am I the worst?</i>

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.710
Rinne-sama.

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:19.220
Forgive me, Rokumon. 
This doesn't warrant hesitation.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.260
Guys, I have...

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.110
He put his blood and sweat 
into buying that cake,

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.890
and he's going to use it to save us.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:28.440
I think we should get that chicken.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.640
Yeah, since we don't have any cake.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.740
Rokudou-kun, help us out.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.320
The chicken, right? Got it.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:38.330
<i>You're going to hide it until 
the very end, huh, Rinne-sama?</i>

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.320
Ageha, that message tube 
you called me out with...

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.950
You launched it from this house, right?

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.080
Oh, I see.

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:50.210
That means that tools and 
stuff can get in and out.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.970
Piece of cake, then.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.440
We're dragging it over, right?

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.890
All right, pull!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.920
Chicken bones are bad for dogs and cats...

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.910
Jumonji! It's your fault!

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:18.760
Shut up! Take this!

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.900
Stop it, stupid!

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:22.980
Holy Ash!

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.440
Holy Ash!

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.700
At least use these.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.580
<i>Will I have to use the cake?</i>

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:37.340
Hello! Christmas tree delivery, as ordered!

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:41.340
The cake!

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.360
What?

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.470
Cake?!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.330
Merry Christmas!

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.740
The tree and everything else vanished.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.000
It's as if it took it to the afterlife.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:14.330
I guess it was content 
with everything it got.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.130
The cake... The cake I bled 150 yen for...

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.910
It was a lie; you had cake. 
Why didn't you hand it over?

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:31.700
Shut up! You would never 
understand how it feels not to be

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.440
part of any Christmas festivities any more.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.530
You wanted to celebrate Christmas <i>that</i> badly?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.320
Then, if it's all right with you...

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.070
What? No!

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:42.030
No, you don't!

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:46.390
Hey, Rinne, why don't we all 
have an actual party, then?

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.680
Oh, yeah. What do you say, Mamiya-san?

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.950
Let's have a party.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.830
I wouldn't mind.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.960
P-Party?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.660
Yeah, Rinne.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.260
The sun only just set.

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:00.130
Christmas Eve is just getting started.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.450
<i>Yup, it's just getting started.</i>

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:07.390
<i>I'd forgotten because of all the 
panic, but I still have that thing.</i>

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.640
<i>The ultimate weapon of bonding 
between a man and a woman.</i>

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.370
<i>I have the Friendly Square!</i>

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:22.980
It's cold.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:26.320
I have to make preparations. See you later.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:32.490
I hate to lose the party, but wouldn't 
everyone freeze at your place?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:36.020
That's why I'm gathering 
all these newspapers.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.290
They're perfectly warm once 
you get used to them.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.710
<i>It's... It's...</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.630
<i>Ko... Ko...</i>

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:48.790
<i>A kotatsu!</i>

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.600
Welcome home, Rinne.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.610
Am I dreaming?

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:57.140
A super-high value heating device 
— a kotatsu — in my room?!

00:13:57.490 --> 00:14:00.400
Wait, so do you not get power here?

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.520
Leave it to me.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:09.180
I brought power from a lamp 
post in the afterlife.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.280
<i>How cooperative, foolish black cat.</i>

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.430
<i>You don't even know that this is what'll</i>

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:16.410
<i>create an Intimacy Field between me and Rinne:</i>

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:19.410
<i>a Friendly Square!</i>

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.790
<i>It's just a kotatsu.</i>

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.560
<i>I'll say it again, since it's important:</i>

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:27.050
<i>It's just a kotatsu.</i>

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:40.660
<i>"Instructions: Once you lure your 
target into the Intimacy Field,</i>

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:45.200
<i>attempt to establish contact by holding 
hands or playing with their feet."</i>

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.440
<i>Okay.</i>

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.140
<i>Hand... Hand...</i>

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.950
Ageha... I mean, Ageha-sama...

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.660
Sorry I've been treating you like 
you're kind of an idiot until now.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:03.850
Rokumon, don't be rude to Ageha-sama.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.890
You've been treating me 
like I'm kind of an idiot?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:10.780
Ahem.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.480
<i>Yay, he's not resisting!</i>

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:23.050
<i>I feel like I'm being touched.</i>

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:26.950
<i>Oh, well. I don't care.</i>

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:31.770
<i>I don't want to move anymore, no matter what.</i>

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:38.120
About the cake, they just sold out, 
so they're going to make us some more.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.620
Let's warm up with oden for now.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:41.890
Oden, huh?

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:42.130
Shi—

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.770
Thank you, Mamiya Sakura.

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.130
Hey, a kotatsu.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.750
It's heavy!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.790
Huh, she's already here?

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.080
Y-Yeah.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:54.230
Oh? Rokudou the hobo has a kotatsu.

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:57.320
Tsubasa-kun, you brought us chicken.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:58.310
It's a do-over.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.440
Okay, let's all have oden 
and chicken in the kotatsu.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.350
Why are you making the calls?!

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.650
'cause it's cold.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:06.910
'cause it's a kotatsu.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.650
Kotatsu this, kotatsu that...

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.890
This is a—

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.460
"This is a"?

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:15.240
Actually, let's just say it's a kotatsu.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.520
<i>It's a kotatsu.</i>

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.500
This is so relaxing.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.430
<i>My Friendly Square's for nothing!</i>

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.090
<i>When are these guys leaving?</i>

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.670
<i>That scarf from earlier 
should be in that bag.</i>

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:34.000
<i>How should I find out who it's for?</i>

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.600
All right, let's play cards.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.180
You have a deck?

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:43.600
I do card reading-ish things for work.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.470
I only know how to play Old Maid.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:47.900
Let's play that, then.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.150
We might as well bet on something.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.090
I don't have a single yen to wager.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:56.030
Yeah, I know.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:56.660
So then...

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.700
Okay, I say the loser has to do 
whatever everyone else says.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.080
<i>Nice, Ageha!</i>

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:08.840
Let's go.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.340
I lost!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.590
Sakura, go home!

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:15.980
Crap, I lost!

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.510
Jumonji, leave!

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.370
I lost.

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.190
Rinne, marry me!

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:24.270
I win!

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.630
Why would you lose to a cat?

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.600
F-Fine.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.040
I'm listening.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:35.400
Go buy us drinks then, please.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.160
Orange
 With pulp

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.400
Let's go for round two.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:46.040
You're going down this time.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.450
I win!

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:50.970
You're bad at this.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.590
Yay! Yay!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.170
Taiyaki

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.170
Tai

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.050
<i>Not this time!</i>

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:05.930
Am I good or what?

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.940
Convenience

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.930
<i>Next time, I swear!</i>

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.990
Looks like I win.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.960
So? What do you want me to do?

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.630
I don't expect anything more of you.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.250
Just tell me.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:38.200
Oh, yeah, Sakura-sama. You said 
you were going to get cake later.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.380
Cake!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.730
Fine.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:46.140
Thank you.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.140
<i>Something's not right.</i>

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:51.650
<i>I can't get intimate at all.</i>

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.770
<i>Wait...</i>

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.820
<i>Is the Friendly Square a scam?!</i>

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:04.640
Hey, I can't help but feel bad for Ageha.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:09.370
But she's the one that 
keeps asking for a rematch.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:13.090
She hates to lose, but she's hilariously bad.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.810
Even I don't feel good about it.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:22.440
Man, it's cold, even with the kotatsu.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.450
No wonder it's cold.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:27.140
Look.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.420
Snow.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:32.790
<i>He tricked me!</i>

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:37.300
<i>Damn it! I'll destroy that piece of crap!</i>

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:02.800
<i>I wanted to have a fun Christmas with Rinne.</i>

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.330
<i>Why does everyone get in my way?</i>

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:11.610
Merry Christmas.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.210
Rinne.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:19.270
This...

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.150
Merry Christmas.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.660
Merry Christmas, Ageha.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.200
Merry Christmas.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.630
We all get one?

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.530
Yeah.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:33.330
My mom's hooked on knitting these days.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.830
She made one for everyone.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:39.090
Mamiya's Mom (39)

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.230
She'd be happy if you'd have it.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.590
It's warm, though.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:50.720
It must have been cold.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:52.670
Let's go.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.600
Okay.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.490
Now, warm up.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.740
<i>Rinne's being nice.</i>

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.980
Sorry we kept making you get us stuff.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.700
It must have been cold outside.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.320
<i>Everyone's kind of nice, too.</i>

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.470
<i>Actually, this is a gaze of pity.</i>

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:33.780
<i>Huh, so is the Friendly Square real?</i>

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:38.230
Come on, it won't taste any 
different if it's squashed.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.170
Let's eat.

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:56.620
Was that—

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:57.580
What?

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:02.710
Yum.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:08.610
<i>And that's how we spent our Christmas Eve.</i>

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:15.190
Hey, we should go home now.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:16.290
I'm sleepy.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:18.040
We're playing until I win.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.980
When are you going to win?

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:24.940
<i>It wasn't a very holy night at all,</i>

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:29.560
<i>but I think we all ended up a 
little closer because of it.</i>

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:25.980
Next Episode:
Fox Trap

00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:04.200
I wonder what happens when 
you get possessed by a fox.

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:05.730
I think you get <i>con</i>fused.

00:24:05.730 --> 00:24:06.370
Confused?

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:07.720
You start liking <i>con</i>servative colors;

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:08.720
you <i>con</i>sume nothing but <i>corn</i>,

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:09.720
your throat gets <i>con</i>gested,

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:11.060
you become a <i>con</i>nosieur 
of <i>com</i>edy and <i>com</i>puters.

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:13.930
Because foxes are <i>con</i> artists?

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:16.180
Foxes aren't that stupid, though.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.900
You probably wouldn't realize 
you're possessed right away.

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:19.830
Con, con.

00:24:19.830 --> 00:24:22.700
Next time on <i>Rin-ne</i>:
"Fox Trap."

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:23.980
Enjoycon.

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:25.980
I just heard you say "con."
